- **Rainy day walk:** Take a leisurely walk in a park or nature preserve, enjoying the sounds and smells of the rain. Be sure to wear waterproof clothing and shoes.
- **Visit a museum or art gallery:** Spend the day indoors exploring a local museum or art gallery. Many museums offer free or discounted admission on certain days of the week.
- **Go to a movie theater:** Catch a new release or a classic film at a local movie theater.
- **Play indoor games:** Have a game night with friends or family, playing board games, card games, or video games.
- **Go bowling:** Enjoy a few rounds of bowling at a local bowling alley.
- **Visit an indoor playground:** If you have young children, take them to an indoor playground where they can run, climb, and play in a safe and supervised environment.
- **Go shopping:** Browse the shops at a local mall or shopping center.
- **Have a picnic lunch:** Pack a lunch and find a spot indoors or under a covered shelter to enjoy a meal.
- **Go to a coffee shop or bookstore:** Curl up with a good book or sip on a warm drink at a local coffee shop or bookstore.
